        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "This agreement between CWA, IBEW and Lucent Technologies addresses Union organizing and consent elections in those job titles and occupations in Lucent organizations that are not covered by the 1988 Union-Management Relations Agreement, separately attached hereto. It is effective on July 1, 1998.",
            "block_bbox": [
                319,
                284,
                875,
                356
            ],
            "block_id": 4,
            "block_order": 2,
            "group_id": 4,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    319.0,
                    284.0
                ],
                [
                    875.0,
                    284.0
                ],
                [
                    875.0,
                    356.0
                ],
                [
                    319.0,
                    356.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "As recognized by their participation in Work Place of the Future, and as a part thereof, the Unions and the Company recognize that it is in their mutual interest to operate in the spirit of partnership and common vision. The parties also share the mutual goals of building a world class, high performance enterprise and addressing employment security through business success and employee development.",
            "block_bbox": [
                320,
                360,
                875,
                465
            ],
            "block_id": 5,
            "block_order": 3,
            "group_id": 5,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    320.0,
                    360.0
                ],
                [
                    875.0,
                    360.0
                ],
                [
                    875.0,
                    465.0
                ],
                [
                    320.0,
                    465.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "The parties also recognize the Unions' goal of growing membership. In order to maintain this perspective and to also avoid unnecessary confrontation, the parties agree that the following principles regarding neutrality and consent election will be applicable to all wholly owned Lucent Business Operating Groups and Divisions throughout the country and shall be the exclusive means by which the Unions, their locals, or individuals acting on their behalf, will conduct an effort to organize non-management employees in the covered Lucent Business Operating Groups or Divisions.",
            "block_bbox": [
                320,
                470,
                875,
                611
            ],
            "block_id": 6,
            "block_order": 4,
            "group_id": 6,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    320.0,
                    470.0
                ],
                [
                    875.0,
                    470.0
                ],
                [
                    875.0,
                    611.0
                ],
                [
                    320.0,
                    611.0
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "paragraph_title",
            "block_content": "1 Employee Choice",
            "block_bbox": [
                321,
                635,
                487,
                653
            ],
            "block_id": 7,
            "block_order": 5,
            "group_id": 7,
            "block_polygon_points": [
                [
                    320.99993896484375,
                    634.9999389648438
                ],
                [
                    485.99993896484375,
                    634.9999389648438
                ],
                [
                    485.99993896484375,
                    651.9999389648438
                ],
                [
                    320.99993896484375,
                    651.9999389648438
                ]
            ]
        },
        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "Both the Unions and the Company support and agree with the principle that the decision as to whether or not to become represented by a Union is one that does not belong to either the Union or to the Company. Rather, it is an individual decision that belongs to the employee. With the parties' mutual recognition of this fundamental tenet, the following provisions are intended to establish, encourage, and nurture an environment during a Union organizing drive that will allow employees to choose whether or not to become represented in a fully informed and uncoerced manner. All negotiations concerning appropriate unit, access, conduct, and voting will be performed by local management and local Union officials, i.e., those directly impacted by these discussions. The local Union and management officials may request a meeting with the appropriate Union and Company headquarters representatives at the beginning of this process.",
            "block_bbox": [
                353,
                660,
                876,
                887
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 6,
            "group_id": 8,
